  "database": "rschema_0447",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0447 database is designed to manage user information, financial documents, and system configuration, as well as track notifications and document management activities. The User table stores details about each user, including their associated unit, password, phone number, role, unique user ID, and username. The Financial_Document table contains information about financial documents, such as the attachment path, category, content, ID, level, number, title, issue date, issuing unit, remarks, and validity status. The Notification table keeps track of notifications sent to users, including the issue date, content, ID, status, title, and the user who received the notification, with a foreign key referencing the User table to establish the relationship between notifications and users. The System_Configuration table stores system-wide settings, including the admin ID, configuration ID, data type, database directory, file upload directory, and system name, with a foreign key referencing the User table to link the admin to their user account. The Document_Management table tracks document management activities, including the admin ID, document ID, operation time, and operation type, with composite primary key constraints on both admin ID and document ID to uniquely identify each activity, and foreign keys referencing the User and Financial_Document tables to link the activity to the user and document involved.",
  "gold_question": "Requirements:\n1.User Information Management: Each registered user in the financial system has a unique user ID, username, password, phone number, associated unit, and role.\n2.Financial Document Management: Collect and organize financial systems, accounting treatment FAQs, accounting practice tips, and other materials. Each financial document includes the document title, document number, issuing unit, issue date, document category, document level, validity status, remarks, document content, and attachment path. Administrators can perform operations on the document, recording the operation time and type.\n3.Notification Management: Users can publish notifications. The content of the notification includes the notification content, issue date, and notification status.\n4.Web System Configuration: Administrators can perform operations such as adding, modifying, or deleting database content. The configuration records the system name, database directory, data type, and file upload directory.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0447.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0447\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `unit` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `financial_document` (\n  `document_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `attachment_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `issue_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `issuing_unit` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `validity_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`document_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notification` (\n  `notification_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `issue_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notification_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system_configuration` (\n  `configuration_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `data_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `database_directory` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `file_upload_directory` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `system_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`configuration_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `system_configuration_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`admin_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `document_management` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `document_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`, `document_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `document_management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`admin_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `document_management_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`document_id`) REFERENCES `financial_document` (`document_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
